WEBVTT

00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:05.350
<v NARRATOR>This was a lofty chamber, lined
and littered with countless bottles.

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:11.490
Broad, low tables were scattered about,
which bristled with retorts, test-tubes,

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:14.930
and little Bunsen lamps, with their blue
flickering flames.

00:00:16.557 --> 00:00:20.937
<v NARRATOR>There was only one student in
the room, who was bending over a distant

00:00:20.937 --> 00:00:26.977
table absorbed in his work. At the sound
of our steps he glanced round and sprang

00:00:26.977 --> 00:00:29.197
to his feet with a cry of pleasure.

00:00:30.682 --> 00:00:32.142
<v HOLMES>I've found it! I've found it!

00:00:33.711 --> 00:00:35.511
<v NARRATOR>he shouted to my companion,

00:00:36.171 --> 00:00:38.791
running towards us with a test-tube in his
hand.

00:00:40.312 --> 00:00:42.052
<v HOLMES>I have found a re-agent which is

00:00:42.052 --> 00:00:44.572
precipitated by haemoglobin, and by
nothing else.

00:00:46.337 --> 00:00:48.357
<v NARRATOR>Had he discovered a gold mine,

00:00:48.777 --> 00:00:51.657
greater delight could not have shone upon
his features.

00:00:53.406 --> 00:00:55.686
<v STAMFORD>Doctor Watson, Mister Sherlock
Holmes,

00:00:57.411 --> 00:00:59.411
<v NARRATOR>said Stamford, introducing us.

00:01:00.877 --> 00:01:01.717
<v HOLMES>How are you?

00:01:03.071 --> 00:01:07.951
<v NARRATOR>he said cordially, gripping my
hand with a strength for which I should

00:01:07.951 --> 00:01:09.511
hardly have given him credit.

00:01:11.285 --> 00:01:14.005
<v HOLMES>You have been in Afghanistan, I
perceive.

00:01:16.066 --> 00:01:17.606
<v NARRATOR>How on earth did you know that?

00:01:18.956 --> 00:01:20.436
<v NARRATOR>I asked in astonishment.

00:01:21.935 --> 00:01:23.215
<v HOLMES>Never mind,

00:01:24.825 --> 00:01:26.365
<v NARRATOR>said he, chuckling to himself.
